Alembic revisions for the HRMS Postgres schema.

The database URL is not in alembic.ini — migrations/env.py takes it from the
app settings, so migrations always run against the database the app is
configured for and credentials live in one place.

  alembic upgrade head              apply everything outstanding
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add x"   after changing a model
  alembic check                     is the schema in sync with the models?
  alembic downgrade -1              step back one revision
  alembic history --verbose         what exists and in what order

Always read an autogenerated revision before applying it. Autogenerate is good
at tables, columns and indexes; it does not see data migrations, and it will
happily generate a column drop that throws away rows.
